senses.gloss:
mucilinda (in mgs. 1—3 also mahā-muc˚; in mgs. 1—4 = Pali mucalinda, which Geiger 〔34〕 assumes was ‘more original’ than muci˚, perh. because of Pali mucala; but I see no convincing ground for preferring either to the other),
(1) n. of a tree (m.) and its flower (nt.): Mv 〔ii.60.18〕 (vs; read mucilinda-ketakā, see Pali Jāt 〔v.405.24〕); ˚dā (n. pl.) ca ketakā 〔ii.254.7〕; ˚da- (in comp.) 〔iii.80.11〕; LV 〔11.1〕; ˚dam, nt. (the flower), Mvy 〔6167〕;
(2) n. of a mountain (= Pali Muca˚ 6 in DPPN): SP 〔244.10—11〕; Samādh 〔19.19〕; Sukh 〔63.3〕; Kv 〔91.12〕;
(3) n. of a nāga king (= Pali Muca˚ 2 in DPPN) who protected the Buddha in a celebrated incident told LV 〔379.15 ff.〕; Mv 〔iii.300.16 ff.〕; referred to as a nāga, or nāga king, Suv 〔162.9〕; Mmk 〔241.17〕; 〔452.17〕; Megh 〔288.6〕; Māy 〔222.5〕; 〔246.31〕;
(4) n. of an ancient king (cakravartin), prob. = Pali Muca˚ 1 or 3 in DPPN: Mvy 〔3563〕; cf. also Pali Mucala, DPPN;
(5) n. of an asura prince: Mv 〔iii.138.2〕; 〔254.9〕; cf. Mucila.
